Runtime: SDD

Purpose:
  Agent runtime state and execution context. Tracks current agent,
  session, events, and checkpoints during chain execution.

Owns: ./

ReadOrder:
   1 @INDEX.sdd
   2 @execution.sdd (execution engine and state machine)
   3 @events.sdd (runtime event log)
   4 @context.sdd (context engine and knowledge resolution)

Rules:
  [RT1] Runtime state MUST be preserved across chain stages.
  [RT2] Checkpoints MUST be created before risky operations.
  [RT3] Events MUST be logged for audit trail.
  [RT4] Execution state persists in DB, not RAM.
  [RT5] Crash recovery MUST resume from exact state, not restart.
  [RT6] Agent state MUST be persisted after each step.
  [RT7] Context MUST be minimal and relevant — never full project dump.
  [RT8] Events are immutable and append-only.
  [RT9] Event ordering is guaranteed per execution_id.
  [RT10] Agent MUST NOT add signatures or sign-offs to runtime outputs.
  [RT11] Agent MUST NOT use emojis, icons, or decorative symbols in runtime output headers or titles.

Navigation:
  Runtime: @INDEX.sdd
  Execution: @execution.sdd
  Events: @events.sdd
  Context: @context.sdd
  Agent: @state.sdd
  Session: @state.sdd
  Current: @state.sdd
  Adapter: @adapter-runtime.sdd
  Checkpoints: @../patterns/checkpoint-restore.sdd
  Orchestrator: @../orchestrator/INDEX.sdd
  Protocol: @../protocol/INDEX.sdd
  State: @../standards/states.sdd

State: +
